WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:11.369
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the twentieth. Have we got everyone on? Reidy, your picture's frozen, but that's fairly normal.</v>

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.939
<v Callum Reid>I'm here. That's just my enthusiastic face.</v>

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:25.559
<v Hannah Price>Morning. The heating in the portakabin is actually working for once. I'm sat here in a coat, absolutely roasting. Not a maintenance request, before anyone says it.</v>

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.719
<v Marcus Hale>Luxury. Usually warmer stood outside it.</v>

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.890
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, well, apparently we've gone straight from refrigeration to kiln.</v>

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:44.119
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on important matters, the charity bake sale on Friday. Saw the poster coming in. Reckon there'll be anything left by our break?</v>

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:47.530
<v Jamie Brennan>Not if you get there first, Marc.</v>

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:56.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cake forecast noted. Actual plant stuff. I already swapped the filter on the big board yesterday, so that's finished, not another job.</v>

00:00:56.909 --> 00:01:00.759
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, the filter change is closed. Separate from the purchasing bit.</v>

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:10.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. And I signed off the inspection on the big board on Tuesday — earlier this morning, I mean. That's done as well.</v>

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:18.019
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I finished the repair on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot last night. That's complete.</v>

00:01:19.069 --> 00:01:21.870
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, Mide, you clipped out. Finished, you said?</v>

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.950
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Finished, yeah. Not carrying that repair forward.</v>

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:37.870
<v Hannah Price>Just an observation from me: saw the pressure on the power pack on one dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Nothing further to add to that.</v>

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:44.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observation only. We're not turning that into an action on this call.</v>

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:56.299
<v Jamie Brennan>Similar thing, different kit — saw the pressure on the heater box on one dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Just mentioning what I saw.</v>

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.969
<v Aisha Begum>Right, two separate observations, then. Not one fault with two names.</v>

00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:10.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Blocked items: the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the tower. That remains blocked; no new action against it here.</v>

00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:17.580
<v Callum Reid>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT1 compressor. Same situation, still blocked.</v>

00:02:19.949 --> 00:02:26.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Also, the shutdown on the stacker is cancelled now, production need it running. Take that out of the picture.</v>

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:33.639
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, cancelled. We're not treating that as shutdown work still waiting to happen.</v>

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Reidy, can you inspect the GT2 water valve for leaks?</v>

00:02:39.849 --> 00:02:43.699
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll inspect the GT2 water valve for leaks. That's mine.</v>

00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:49.310
<v Marcus Hale>The valve itself, yeah? Not getting muddled with the compressor item we've just mentioned.</v>

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:54.800
<v Callum Reid>No, separate thing entirely. Inspection for leaks, as asked.</v>

00:02:56.479 --> 00:03:04.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Reidy, can you also do a site visit at the water works with the contractor at half two? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:05.189 --> 00:03:12.539
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that one, sorry. Can't get off the floor for that slot. The valve's fine, but not the visit.</v>

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:22.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Ash, can you take the site visit at the water works with the contractor instead? Still at half two; it matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:30.340
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I'll do the site visit at the water works with the contractor at half two. That works for me.</v>

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:36.319
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Ash. Sorry, should've said before you got all the way through it.</v>

00:03:37.729 --> 00:03:42.629
<v Sarah Okafor>No bother. I'll run a function test on the line 2 guard tomorrow morning.</v>

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.159
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Saz, is that a drop-everything one, or a whenever you get a chance sort of thing?</v>

00:03:51.460 --> 00:04:00.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Whenever you get a chance is the priority on that one, yeah. I'll fit the function test on the line 2 guard into tomorrow morning.</v>

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:05.120
<v Hannah Price>Right, tomorrow morning, but not top of the queue. Got you.</v>

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:12.460
<v Sarah Okafor>Ash, could you chase the purchase order for the big board after lunch? No rush.</v>

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:22.879
<v Aisha Begum>Um, can I pass on that? With the visit in the afternoon, I don't want to say yes and then leave it hanging.</v>

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:31.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Fair enough. Marc, can you take that instead — chase the purchase order for the big board after lunch? No rush.</v>

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.930
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll chase the purchase order for the big board after lunch. No rush, understood.</v>

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:45.629
<v Jamie Brennan>And that's the purchase order, not reordering the filter that's already been changed. Just keeping those separate in my head.</v>

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:51.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Jamie, can you order spare parts for the HRSG tomorrow? Normal priority.</v>

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:56.279
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll order spare parts for the HRSG tomorrow, normal priority.</v>

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.639
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, talked over the end there. Heard you now.</v>

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:08.389
<v Jamie Brennan>No worries. Teams does that little pause and then gives you everyone at once, doesn't it?</v>

00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:15.870
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on the plant, I'll grease and check the bearings on the Gas Turbine 1 by Thursday.</v>

00:05:16.779 --> 00:05:21.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Ash. For that one, not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:28.250
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, by Thursday. I'll keep that date; I'm not treating it as an emergency.</v>

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:35.430
<v Marcus Hale>Right. Different status to the blocked delivery, then. Easy to mash those together when you're half listening.</v>

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:40.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Mide, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team? Normal priority.</v>

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.029
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team. Normal priority, got it.</v>

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.699
<v Callum Reid>You always sound delighted when we say toolbox talk.</v>

00:05:53.649 --> 00:05:57.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>This is my delighted voice. Same model as your enthusiastic face.</v>

00:05:58.029 --> 00:06:02.579
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances on Friday. It's urgent.</v>

00:06:03.149 --> 00:06:08.399
<v Hannah Price>Boss, just so I've heard that properly — urgent, but the checks are on Friday?</v>

00:06:09.189 --> 00:06:16.540
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, on Friday, before use. I'll do the pre-use checks on the counterbalances myself. It's urgent, not one to squeeze out.</v>

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.660
<v Marcus Hale>So cake doesn't outrank it. Glad we've established the hierarchy.</v>

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:25.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Cake has never outranked it, despite your best efforts.</v>

00:06:25.939 --> 00:06:35.040
<v Hannah Price>And just to keep my bit tidy, that pressure dip I mentioned was an observation, not me asking for another job to go on the list.</v>

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:41.399
<v Jamie Brennan>Same for mine. It recovered on its own; I wasn't volunteering anybody for anything.</v>

00:06:43.709 --> 00:06:48.959
<v Callum Reid>Supplier delivery still in the blocked column as well. Nothing's changed during the call, unfortunately.</v>

00:06:50.899 --> 00:06:56.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Those stay blocked, the stacker shutdown stays cancelled, and the finished repairs stay finished.</v>

00:06:57.019 --> 00:07:00.170
<v Aisha Begum>Lovely. A closed job actually staying closed. Rare treat.</v>

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:05.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Did we lose the last bit, or has everyone gone quiet?</v>

00:07:05.839 --> 00:07:08.290
<v Jamie Brennan>Just quiet. Enjoy it while it lasts.</v>

00:07:08.629 --> 00:07:10.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:13.939
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
